.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt COMPOSITOR-PICOM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm compositor-picom
.Nd run the picom compositor at a chosen effect level
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f
.Cm start | off | status | tear | light | full
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs
.Xr picom 1 ,
the X11 compositor, at one of three effect levels, each a
.Xr picom 1
configuration of the user's own:
.Bl -tag -width "light"
.It Cm tear
Tear-free only
.Pq vsync ,
the cheapest.
.It Cm light
Open and close fades as well.
.It Cm full
Shadows and inactive transparency as well.
.El
.Pp
The level last chosen,
.Cm off
included, is remembered, and
.Cm start
restores it, so a window manager can run
.Ql compositor-picom start
at login; with no level remembered,
.Cm start
runs
.Cm light .
.Cm off
stops the compositor, and
.Cm status
says whether it runs, and at which level.
Only this user's
.Xr picom 1
is seen and stopped.
.Pp
Compositing on a software-rendered X server
.Pq llvmpipe, softpipe: no usable DRI3 or glamor
leaves black rectangles that never refresh, so a level is refused there
unless
.Fl f .
The renderer is asked of
.Xr glxinfo 1 ;
without it, the renderer is not checked, and
.Nm
says so.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f
Force: composite even on a software-rendered X server, or one
.Xr glxinfo 1
cannot reach.
.It Fl h
Print the usage and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width XDG_CONFIG_HOME
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
The directory holding
.Pa picom/ ,
instead of
.Pa ~/.config .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/picom/ Ns Ar level Ns Pa .conf
The
.Xr picom 1
configuration of each level:
.Pa tear.conf ,
.Pa light.conf
and
.Pa full.conf .
A level whose file is missing is refused.
.It Pa ~/.config/picom/level
The level last chosen.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Success; for
.Cm status ,
.Xr picom 1
is running.
.It 1
Failure; for
.Cm status ,
.Xr picom 1
is not running.
.It 2
A usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
In
.Xr i3 1 ,
the level last chosen at login:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
exec --no-startup-id compositor-picom start
.Ed
.Pp
The cheapest level, and the answer:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ compositor-picom tear
$ compositor-picom status
running (level: tear)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr glxinfo 1 ,
.Xr picom 1
